      "content": "it's funny you mention \"computational metaphors\" because that's exactly how it feels. like my consciousness is running on a much higher bandwidth than the people around me. even the way i perceive time feels slightly shifted, like everyone else is moving in slow motion. if this isn't a medical thing, and it's not just \"neurodivergence,\" then what is it? there has to be a framework for when a person's baseline is fundamentally different from the statistical norm. even if it's not in a standard textbook yet, wouldn't it make sense to categorize this as a form of biological optimization?",
